---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About & Leadership — Veloxcore">

<!-- ── HERO ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="about-hero" data-screen-label="01 Hero">
  <canvas class="hero-canvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="page-eyebrow">Who we are</div>
        <h1 class="hero-h1">The engineering studio that ships <em>AI</em> for serious companies.</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">Founded in 2012 in Ahmedabad. Built on a decade of Azure data engineering. Now AI-native — shipping agentic systems and building our own AI products.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-right">
        <div class="hero-stat-row">
          <div class="h-stat"><div class="h-stat-num">2012</div><div class="h-stat-label">Year founded</div></div>
          <div class="h-stat"><div class="h-stat-num">UN</div><div class="h-stat-label">Among our clients</div></div>
          <div class="h-stat"><div class="h-stat-num">10+ yrs</div><div class="h-stat-label">Azure depth</div></div>
          <div class="h-stat"><div class="h-stat-num">1</div><div class="h-stat-label">AI product shipped</div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="partner-badge reveal">
          <div class="partner-logo-box">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 23 23"><path d="M1 1h10v10H1z" fill="#f25022"/><path d="M12 1h10v10H12z" fill="#7fba00"/><path d="M1 12h10v10H1z" fill="#00a4ef"/><path d="M12 12h10v10H12z" fill="#ffb900"/></svg>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="partner-text-main">Microsoft Solutions Partner</div>
            <div class="partner-text-sub">Data &amp; AI · Digital &amp; App Innovation</div>
          </div>
          <div class="partner-badge-pill">Certified</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── STORY ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="story" data-screen-label="02 Story">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="story-grid">
      <div class="reveal">
        <div class="story-label">Our story</div>
        <h2 class="story-h">Built for depth, not breadth.</h2>
        <p class="story-p">Veloxcore was founded in 2012 in Ahmedabad by Vinit B Yadav — an engineer who had spent years inside enterprise data teams, watching the same problems repeat: pipelines that broke silently, dashboards that were three days stale, ML models that never made it to production. The company started to fix that — not with a new tool, but with better engineering practice.</p>
        <p class="story-p">For the first decade, we focused on the <strong>Microsoft Azure data platform</strong> — Event Hubs, HDInsight, Data Factory, Stream Analytics, Power BI — and earned Microsoft Solutions Partner status in <strong>Data &amp; AI</strong> and <strong>Digital &amp; App Innovation</strong>. We went deep. Enterprise engagements ranged from mid-market retail to the <strong>United Nations</strong>.</p>
        <p class="story-p">In 2023, the world changed. LLMs became production-viable, and every enterprise client we served started asking the same question: <em>how do we actually ship AI?</em> We had a clear answer — because we had the data infrastructure, the Azure depth, and the engineering discipline to build AI systems that work in production, not just in demos. We proved it by building our own: <strong>Veloxhire.AI</strong>, an agentic AI interview platform launched in 2024. In July 2025, Vinit took the story to the wider .NET community at <strong>Dot Net Day Ahmedabad</strong>, presenting <em>"Building Agents with MCP"</em> to 200+ engineers.</p>
        <p class="story-p">That's who we are. An engineering studio that ships AI for serious companies — and eats its own cooking.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal" style="transition-delay:.1s">
        <div class="story-label">Timeline</div>
        <div class="story-right">
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">2012</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <div class="timeline-title">Founded in Ahmedabad</div>
              <div class="timeline-desc">Vinit B Yadav founds Veloxcore to bring engineering discipline to enterprise data work on the Microsoft stack.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">2015–2020</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <div class="timeline-title">Azure data platform years</div>
              <div class="timeline-desc">Big-data and BI engagements on Hadoop, Spark, HDInsight, Stream Analytics, Power BI and Tableau. Microsoft partnership deepens.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">2021</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <div class="timeline-title">Veloxcore Pvt Ltd incorporated</div>
              <div class="timeline-desc">Formal incorporation of the operating entity in India as the team scales beyond founder-led delivery.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">2023</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <div class="timeline-title">United Nations engagement</div>
              <div class="timeline-desc">Veloxcore ships a document-intelligence solution for the UN — one of several international engagements built on our data + AI stack.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">2024</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <div class="timeline-title">Launched Veloxhire.AI</div>
              <div class="timeline-desc">Our first AI product — an agentic interview platform built on Azure OpenAI. The proof that we don't just consult on AI; we ship it.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">2025</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <div class="timeline-title">Agents &amp; MCP, on stage</div>
              <div class="timeline-desc">Vinit presents <em>"Building Agents with MCP"</em> at the 9th Dot Net Day Ahmedabad to 200+ engineers — and we formally reposition around agentic AI.</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── PRINCIPLES ─────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="principles" data-screen-label="03 Principles">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="principles-h reveal">How we think.</h2>
    <p class="principles-sub reveal">Six principles that govern every engagement, every line of code, every conversation with a client.</p>
    <div class="principles-grid">
      <div class="principle-card reveal">
        <div class="principle-num">01</div>
        <div class="principle-title">Production over demos</div>
        <div class="principle-desc">An AI model that works in a Colab notebook is not an AI product. We measure ourselves by what's running in production at scale — not by what looked good in the presentation.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.06s">
        <div class="principle-num">02</div>
        <div class="principle-title">Honest engineering</div>
        <div class="principle-desc">We tell clients when a problem doesn't need LLMs. We tell clients when their data isn't ready. We'd rather lose a deal than set up an engagement we can't deliver.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.12s">
        <div class="principle-num">03</div>
        <div class="principle-title">Depth, not breadth</div>
        <div class="principle-desc">We don't work in every cloud. We don't support every ML framework. We go very deep on Azure and the Microsoft AI ecosystem because depth compounds in ways that breadth doesn't.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.04s">
        <div class="principle-num">04</div>
        <div class="principle-title">We eat our own cooking</div>
        <div class="principle-desc">Veloxhire.AI is built on the same Azure infrastructure we build for clients. If we recommend a pattern, we've run it in production ourselves. That's not marketing — it's accountability.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.10s">
        <div class="principle-num">05</div>
        <div class="principle-title">Your team, not our dependency</div>
        <div class="principle-desc">Every engagement ends with the client's team owning what we built. Runbooks, documentation, training — the goal is always a handover that doesn't require us to exist.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-card reveal" style="transition-delay:.16s">
        <div class="principle-num">06</div>
        <div class="principle-title">Cost is a feature</div>
        <div class="principle-desc">Cloud cost is part of every architecture decision, not an afterthought. We've reduced client bills by 30–40% post-engagement — because we build systems that are efficient, not just functional.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── LEADERSHIP ─────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="leadership" data-screen-label="04 Leadership">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="lead-header">
      <h2 class="lead-h reveal">Leadership</h2>
      <p class="lead-sub reveal">The people responsible for the work — and available to talk to you directly.</p>
    </div>

